---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { activeStates } from "../data/states";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Reading the Law"
  description="The definitive guide to becoming a lawyer through legal apprenticeship — no law school, no six-figure debt. Learn how California, Vermont, Virginia, and Washington let you read the law."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.06]" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 1px 1px, #fff 1px, transparent 0); background-size: 24px 24px;"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-24 text-center sm:py-32">
      <p class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brass-light text-xs">Reading the Law</p>
      <h1 class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-3xl font-serif text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-parchment sm:text-5xl">
        Become a real, bar-licensed lawyer — without law school debt
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-parchment/75">
        In four U.S. states, you can still become an attorney by apprenticing directly under a practicing
        lawyer or judge instead of attending law school. It's called <strong class="text-parchment">reading the law</strong>,
        and it's exactly how Abraham Lincoln, and thousands of American lawyers before the 20th century, got their start.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row">
        <a href="/what-is-reading-the-law/" class="w-full rounded-sm bg-brass px-7 py-3.5 text-center font-semibold text-navy transition hover:bg-brass-light sm:w-auto">
          Learn How It Works
        </a>
        <a href="/states/" class="w-full rounded-sm border border-parchment/25 px-7 py-3.5 text-center font-semibold text-parchment transition hover:border-parchment/50 sm:w-auto">
          Compare State Programs
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-xs text-parchment/40">
        Not legal advice. Educational information only — see our <a href="/disclaimer/" class="underline hover:text-parchment/70">disclaimer</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Stats bar -->
  <section class="border-b border-navy/10 bg-parchment-dark/60">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-2 gap-6 px-5 py-10 text-center sm:grid-cols-4">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">4</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-light">Pure apprenticeship states</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">2</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-light">Hybrid combination states</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">$0</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-light">Required tuition in CA / VT / VA / WA</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">3–4</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-light">Years of full-time study required</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What is it, short -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-20">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brass">The alternative path</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">
          Law school isn't the only door to the bar exam
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-light">
          Before the American Bar Association standardized legal education around university law schools,
          nearly every lawyer in the country learned the same way: by reading law books and working
          alongside a practicing attorney for several years. That path never disappeared — it's still
          written into the admission rules of California, Vermont, Virginia, and Washington today.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-light">
          Instead of paying law school tuition, you register as a law clerk or "reader," study a
          structured curriculum under a supervising attorney or judge, and — after several years —
          sit for the same state bar examination as any law school graduate. Pass it, and you're a
          licensed attorney with the same license as anyone else.
        </p>
        <a href="/what-is-reading-the-law/" class="mt-6 inline-block font-semibold text-brass hover:text-navy">
          Read the full explainer →
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-navy">This path is not a shortcut</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-light">
          Be honest with yourself before you commit:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-light">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brass">—</span> It takes 3–4 years of genuinely full-time study, the same as law school.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brass">—</span> You must find your own supervising attorney — nobody assigns one to you (yet).</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brass">—</span> Bar passage rates for apprentice-trained candidates run well below ABA law school graduates.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brass">—</span> Your license may only be portable to a limited number of other states.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/faq/" class="mt-5 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-brass hover:text-navy">See the full FAQ →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- States grid -->
  <section class="border-y border-navy/10 bg-parchment-dark/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-20">
      <div class="text-center">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brass">Where it's legal</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">Four states, four different programs</h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-ink-light">
          California, Vermont, Virginia, and Washington each let you skip law school entirely. The rules —
          duration, hours, who can supervise you — vary a lot from state to state.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {
          activeStates.map((state) => (
            <a
              href={`/states/${state.slug}/`}
              class="group rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-white p-6 transition hover:border-brass hover:shadow-md"
            >
              <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-navy group-hover:text-brass">{state.name}</h3>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-brass">{state.programName}</p>
                </div>
                <span class="rounded-full bg-navy/5 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-navy">{state.duration.split(" ")[0]} yrs</span>
              </div>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-light">{state.summary}</p>
              <span class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-brass group-hover:text-navy">
                View {state.name} requirements →
              </span>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 text-center">
        <a href="/states/" class="font-semibold text-brass hover:text-navy">
          See the full state-by-state comparison, plus hybrid programs in Maine and New York →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Matchmaking teaser -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-20">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-10 rounded-xl border border-navy/10 bg-navy px-8 py-12 sm:px-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brass-light">Coming soon</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-parchment sm:text-3xl">
          The hardest part isn't the studying — it's finding a sponsor
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-parchment/70">
          Every program on this site requires you to find your own supervising attorney or judge willing to
          commit years of mentorship. We're building a matchmaking platform to connect aspiring apprentices
          with attorneys open to sponsoring one — so that step stops being the biggest barrier to entry.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-parchment p-6 text-center">
        <p class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-navy">Join the waitlist</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-light">
          Whether you're looking to apprentice or willing to sponsor a reader, get notified when the platform launches.
        </p>
        <a href="/matchmaking/" class="mt-5 inline-block w-full rounded-sm bg-brass px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-navy hover:bg-brass-light">
          Get Early Access →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
